    <h1>01 - ColdFusion basics</h1>
    <p>
        A ColdFusion page is an HTML file with a <code>.cfm</code> extension. The server runs the
        <code>cf</code> tags and sends plain HTML to the browser. These pages use <b>no CSS</b> on
        purpose, so the focus stays on the language.
    </p>

    <p>Read these in order:</p>
    <ol>
        <li><a href="01-syntax.cfm">Syntax</a> - variables, output, data types.</li>
        <li><a href="02-logic.cfm">Logic</a> - if, loops, arrays, structs.</li>
        <li><a href="03-database.cfm">Database</a> - connect and read the <code>pelajar</code> table.</li>
    </ol>

    <p>Full write-up: <code>day1.md</code>, Topics 3-4.</p>
